spes: the picture on the display through sysctl, long GPU submissions in parts, the GPU fault address (0180).

1. debug.spes_fb_shot (root): the pixels the display shows now (the scanned surface or the panel
   memory). Screenshots are black when backboardd draws with Metal; the App Library backdrop and
   the switcher have to be seen to be debugged. "sysctl -b debug.spes_fb_shot > file".
2. RedwoodGPU refused a submission of more than 128 command buffers (App Library's search: 130),
   and backboardd's Vulkan device was lost for good. Up to 4096 are taken now and go to the ring
   128 at a time; the fence is the last part's.
3. The backend's fault report also prints the SMMU fault address and FSYNR0 ('backend stopped:
   fault while waiting for a fence', FSR 0x80000408, cause unknown).

